# /etc/cfm/cfm.dnat_bypass
#
# Source-IP bypass list for the WEB DNAT chain installed by `cfm dnat on`
# (TCP 80 -> HTTP_PORT, TCP+UDP 443 -> HTTPS_PORT). Packets arriving from
# any IP / CIDR listed here SKIP the DNAT redirect and reach Apache /
# LiteSpeed directly, bypassing CFM's openresty/angie challenge + WAF
# layer.
#
# Use sparingly. Typical entries:
#   - cluster peers running the same panel software
#   - backup / monitoring hosts that need raw upstream access
#   - migration source hosts whose transport doesn't tolerate HTTP-aware
#     intermediation
#
# Format (same as cfm.allow / cfm.deny):
#   - one IP or CIDR per line
#   - blank lines and `#`-prefixed lines ignored
#   - trailing `# comment` on data lines also ignored
#   - both IPv4 and IPv6 are supported
#
# Manage with the CLI rather than editing this file by hand:
#   cfm dnat bypass list
#   cfm dnat bypass add    84.54.49.205
#   cfm dnat bypass add    2001:db8::/64
#   cfm dnat bypass remove 84.54.49.205
#
# Changes take effect immediately if web DNAT is currently on; otherwise
# they apply on the next `cfm dnat on`.

# Examples (uncomment to use):
#84.54.49.205         # peer-srv-01
#192.0.2.0/24         # internal management subnet
